{"authored" [{"question" "q-351528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{3/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3130d64d78df001f9aa152331134a47b5741dd9c50120364f6f7d6b82313051" "basis" 1848 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $x\\to {0}^{-}$ and $u\\to 0$ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=\\frac{1}{x}$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $0$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{3/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{0}^{-\\infty }{e}^{3u}\\,\\text{d}u={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{3u}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{3/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}{e}^{3u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{e}^{3u}}{3}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(1-{e}^{3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{3x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{3x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/assets/34abda46dc9fc2c6f14ce4f8460ba076a16004bb9141eb8074cdc08e0c12fd2f.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{3/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}(1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3130d64d78df001f9aa152331134a47b5741dd9c50120364f6f7d6b82313051" "basis" 1848 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60ffd82ac3fcdd824c7b9b52294687f75fc951106566745a06ae384cc170dce2" "basis" 1848 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3130d64d78df001f9aa152331134a47b5741dd9c50120364f6f7d6b82313051" "basis" 1848 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3130d64d78df001f9aa152331134a47b5741dd9c50120364f6f7d6b82313051" "basis" 1848 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056962/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{2}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fa62d5d11bdb4b96bb6baef0f59e1f6f727ea73774ec93f80097f7a913ac704" "basis" 1700 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {b}^{\\,px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p\\operatorname{ln}⁡(b)}{b}^{\\,px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{2}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{2}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{{2}^{-3x}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{2}^{-3x}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{2}^{3a}}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\frac{1}{{2}^{3x}},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{2}^{3x}}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{2}^{3x}}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/assets/998ec723fd7212da4382718750465ce313349ed3f2c0258cc1f68e0a5485d968.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{2}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{2}^{3a}}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (0-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fa62d5d11bdb4b96bb6baef0f59e1f6f727ea73774ec93f80097f7a913ac704" "basis" 1700 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a7daed03fc8c3c14b6f0511b41ff3700c3e15cf58a8b79ca63f477ad77006bf" "basis" 1700 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351559" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fa62d5d11bdb4b96bb6baef0f59e1f6f727ea73774ec93f80097f7a913ac704" "basis" 1700 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{3/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture"